<title>SPAIN: SOCCER-SPANISH FIRST DIVISION LEADING SCORERS.</title>
<headline>SOCCER-SPANISH FIRST DIVISION LEADING SCORERS.</headline>
<dateline>MADRID 1996-11-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>Leading scorers in the Spanish</p>
<p>first division after Sunday's games.</p>
<p>13 -  Ronaldo (Barcelona)</p>
<p>12 -  Davor Suker (Real Madrid)</p>
<p>9  -  Jose Ziganda (Athletic Bilbao)</p>
<p>8  -  Oli Alvarez (Oviedo), Predrag Mijatovic (Real Madrid),</p>
<p>Julen Guerrero (Athletic Bilbao)</p>
<p>7  -  Guilherme (Rayo Vallecano), Juan Eduardo Esnaider </p>
<p>(Atletico Madrid)</p>
<p>6  -  Gustavo Poyet (Zaragoza), Alfonso Perez (Real Betis),</p>
<p>Vladimir Gudelj (Celta Vigo), Salva Ballesta (Sevilla),</p>
<p>Rivaldo (Deportivo Coruna), Raul (Real Madrid),</p>
<p>Alen Peternac (Valldadolid), Gustavo Poyet (Zaragoza),</p>
<p>Manuel Alfaro (Hercules), Julio Salinas (Sporting Gijon).</p>
</text>
